{"t":"2026-05-28T03:43:39.459Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VqtHLnEYxGuknnaLpZb9wL","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-SCORING\n     2→\n     3→> HYPHA tag: `TA/SYNTH-SCORE`\n     4→> Maps to Mycelium agent: `synthetics-scoring-agent`\n     5→\n     6→## Goal\n     7→\n     8→Own the deterministic scoring drift detection harness. Exercise the real `RelevanceScorer` against synthetic candidates and JD fixtures, compute stable fingerprints, compare against accepted baselines, and surface drift reports. This biome is the witness: if Claude changes, if prompts drift, if the archetype generator regresses — the scoring harness sees it within 24 hours.\n     9→\n    10→## Scope\n    11→\n    12→### In Scope\n    13→\n    14→- `backend/synthetics/__init__.py` — module init\n    15→- `backend/synthetics/scoring_runner.py` — `ScoringSyntheticRunner.run_suite()` orchestration\n    16→- `backend/synthetics/fingerprint.py` — `compute_fingerprint(digest, contract)` stable JSON generation\n    17→- `backend/synthetics/diff.py` — `diff_against_baseline(fingerprint, baseline, contract)` → `DriftReport`\n    18→- `backend/synthetics/cli.py` — `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring` CLI entry\n    19→- Cache contract enforcement — verify `cache_control={\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` on every Claude call\n    20→- Cache verification — check `cache_creation_input_tokens == 0` on subsequent runs\n    21→\n    22→### Out of Scope\n    23→\n    24→- Synthetic candidate fixtures (owned by `synthetics-fixtures-agent`)\n    25→- Crawler health monitoring (owned by `synthetics-crawler-agent`)\n    26→- Schema changes — no new tables, no new columns\n    27→- Mocking the Claude API — synthetic INPUTS are mock, the scorer is real\n    28→- Baseline acceptance workflow — that's a future CLI command (`mycelium synthetics baseline accept`)\n    29→\n    30→## Inputs\n    31→\n    32→- `synthetics-fixtures-agent`: Synthetic candidates + JD fixtures\n    33→- `discover-agent` (FROZEN): `RelevanceScorer` class with `score_batch()` method\n    34→- `obs-agent` (FROZEN): `publish_event(channel, payload)` for drift alerts\n    35→- `NUTRIENTS.md §I.2-I.5`: Drift contract fields, baseline management, cache contract\n    36→\n    37→## Outputs (Deliverables)\n    38→\n    39→- `backend/synthetics/__init__.py`\n    40→- `backend/synthetics/scoring_runner.py`\n    41→- `backend/synthetics/fingerprint.py`\n    42→- `backend/synthetics/diff.py`\n    43→- `backend/synthetics/cli.py`\n    44→- `synthetics/runs/` — directory for run output (gitignored)\n    45→- `synthetics/runs/.gitkeep`\n    46→\n    47→## Acceptance Criteria\n    48→\n    49→- [ ] `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring` produces `synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json`\n    50→- [ ] Running the suite twice within 5 minutes produces **identical fingerprints**\n    51→- [ ] Second run shows **>90% cache hit rate** verified from Claude API response usage block\n    52→- [ ] Mutating one JD's text and re-running produces a non-empty `DriftReport` localized to that JD\n    53→- [ ] Mutating one score weight in `relevance_scorer.py` and re-running surfaces drift across all 12 JDs\n    54→- [ ] Every Claude call sets `cache_control={\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` on system prompt + candidate identity\n    55→- [ ] If `cache_creation_input_tokens > 0` on subsequent runs, a `cache_miss` event is written to the report\n    56→- [ ] `agent.status.synthetics.drift` event is published if `DriftReport.severity != 'green'`\n    57→- [ ] No `print()` anywhere — `structlog` only\n    58→- [ ] `ruff check backend/synthetics/` clean\n    59→- [ ] `pytest tests/synthetics/ -v` → exit 0\n    60→\n    61→## Notes\n    62→\n    63→### Run Flow\n    64→\n    65→```\n    66→python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring\n    67→\n    68→1. Load synthetic candidates from database (WHERE id::text LIKE '00000000-%')\n    69→2. Load JD fixtures from synthetics/fixtures/jobs/\n    70→3. For each candidate × JD pair:\n    71→   a. Call RelevanceScorer.score_batch() with cache_control\n    72→   b. Collect score dimensions and composite score\n    73→   c. Track cache hit/miss from response usage\n    74→4. Compute fingerprint per candidate\n    75→5. Load baseline (if exists) from synthetics/fixtures/baselines/\n    76→6. Diff fingerprint against baseline\n    77→7. Write synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json\n    78→8. If drift detected, publish agent.status.synthetics.drift event\n    79→9. Exit 0 (success) or 1 (hard failure only — drift is reported, not failed)\n    80→```\n    81→\n    82→### Fingerprint Stability\n    83→\n    84→The fingerprint MUST be byte-stable across runs. Key decisions:\n    85→\n    86→1. **Sort all arrays by a deterministic key** (job_id for top_picks)\n    87→2. **Round floating-point scores to 4 decimal places** to avoid IEEE precision drift\n    88→3. **Exclude timestamps and run_ids** from fingerprint comparison\n    89→4. **Include ordering of first 5 top_picks** as an exact-match field\n    90→\n    91→### Cache Contract Enforcement\n    92→\n    93→Every Claude API call MUST include:\n    94→\n    95→```python\n    96→messages=[\n    97→    {\n    98→        \"role\": \"user\",\n    99→        \"content\": [\n   100→            {\n   101→                \"type\": \"text\",\n   102→                \"text\": system_prompt,\n   103→                \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}\n   104→            },\n   105→            {\n   106→                \"type\": \"text\",\n   107→                \"text\": candidate_identity,\n   108→                \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}\n   109→            },\n   110→            {\n   111→                \"type\": \"text\",\n   112→                \"text\": jd_text\n   113→            }\n   114→        ]\n   115→    }\n   116→]\n   117→```\n   118→\n   119→The scorer module is FROZEN. If it doesn't support `cache_control`, the synthetics-scoring-agent must call the Claude API directly (bypassing the scorer's internal call) or wrap the scorer with cache-aware instrumentation. Do NOT modify the frozen `relevance_scorer.py`.\n   120→\n   121→### Drift Severity Rules\n   122→\n   123→From NUTRIENTS.md §I.4:\n   124→\n   125→```\n   126→green: zero violations\n   127→yellow: tolerance violations only, no exact-match violations\n   128→red: any exact-match violation OR tolerance violation > 2× threshold\n   129→```\n   130→\n   131→### Report File Path\n   132→\n   133→`synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json`\n   134→\n   135→Where `<ts>` is ISO-8601 UTC timestamp: `2026-05-28T03-00-00Z`\n   136→\n   137→The `synthetics/runs/` directory is gitignored. Reports are ephemeral. Baselines are the permanent record.\n   138→\n   139→### Integration with Celery Beat\n   140→\n   141→The scoring suite runs daily at 03:00 ET. This is NOT wired via scheduler-agent (which is frozen). Instead, synthetics-crawler-agent owns a separate beat schedule extension that additively registers the synthetics tasks.\n   142→\n   143→For this biome (synthetics-scoring-agent), the CLI is the primary interface. Celery scheduling is owned by synthetics-crawler-agent via the additive beat extension.\n   144→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d647432-976a-467b-a023-6b583c162bc9","uuid":"4fb4d237-5817-43da-9fb4-d6c857946348","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/hyphae/HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-SCORING.md","content":"# HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-SCORING\n\n> HYPHA tag: `TA/SYNTH-SCORE`\n> Maps to Mycelium agent: `synthetics-scoring-agent`\n\n## Goal\n\nOwn the deterministic scoring drift detection harness. Exercise the real `RelevanceScorer` against synthetic candidates and JD fixtures, compute stable fingerprints, compare against accepted baselines, and surface drift reports. This biome is the witness: if Claude changes, if prompts drift, if the archetype generator regresses — the scoring harness sees it within 24 hours.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In Scope\n\n- `backend/synthetics/__init__.py` — module init\n- `backend/synthetics/scoring_runner.py` — `ScoringSyntheticRunner.run_suite()` orchestration\n- `backend/synthetics/fingerprint.py` — `compute_fingerprint(digest, contract)` stable JSON generation\n- `backend/synthetics/diff.py` — `diff_against_baseline(fingerprint, baseline, contract)` → `DriftReport`\n- `backend/synthetics/cli.py` — `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring` CLI entry\n- Cache contract enforcement — verify `cache_control={\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` on every Claude call\n- Cache verification — check `cache_creation_input_tokens == 0` on subsequent runs\n\n### Out of Scope\n\n- Synthetic candidate fixtures (owned by `synthetics-fixtures-agent`)\n- Crawler health monitoring (owned by `synthetics-crawler-agent`)\n- Schema changes — no new tables, no new columns\n- Mocking the Claude API — synthetic INPUTS are mock, the scorer is real\n- Baseline acceptance workflow — that's a future CLI command (`mycelium synthetics baseline accept`)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- `synthetics-fixtures-agent`: Synthetic candidates + JD fixtures\n- `discover-agent` (FROZEN): `RelevanceScorer` class with `score_batch()` method\n- `obs-agent` (FROZEN): `publish_event(channel, payload)` for drift alerts\n- `NUTRIENTS.md §I.2-I.5`: Drift contract fields, baseline management, cache contract\n\n## Outputs (Deliverables)\n\n- `backend/synthetics/__init__.py`\n- `backend/synthetics/scoring_runner.py`\n- `backend/synthetics/fingerprint.py`\n- `backend/synthetics/diff.py`\n- `backend/synthetics/cli.py`\n- `synthetics/runs/` — directory for run output (gitignored)\n- `synthetics/runs/.gitkeep`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring` produces `synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json`\n- [ ] Running the suite twice within 5 minutes produces **identical fingerprints**\n- [ ] Second run shows **>90% cache hit rate** verified from Claude API response usage block\n- [ ] Mutating one JD's text and re-running produces a non-empty `DriftReport` localized to that JD\n- [ ] Mutating one score weight in `relevance_scorer.py` and re-running surfaces drift across all 12 JDs\n- [ ] Every Claude call sets `cache_control={\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` on system prompt + candidate identity\n- [ ] If `cache_creation_input_tokens > 0` on subsequent runs, a `cache_miss` event is written to the report\n- [ ] `agent.status.synthetics.drift` event is published if `DriftReport.severity != 'green'`\n- [ ] No `print()` anywhere — `structlog` only\n- [ ] `ruff check backend/synthetics/` clean\n- [ ] `pytest tests/synthetics/ -v` → exit 0\n\n## Notes\n\n### Run Flow\n\n```\npython -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring\n\n1. Load synthetic candidates from database (WHERE id::text LIKE '00000000-%')\n2. Load JD fixtures from synthetics/fixtures/jobs/\n3. For each candidate × JD pair:\n   a. Call RelevanceScorer.score_batch() with cache_control\n   b. Collect score dimensions and composite score\n   c. Track cache hit/miss from response usage\n4. Compute fingerprint per candidate\n5. Load baseline (if exists) from synthetics/fixtures/baselines/\n6. Diff fingerprint against baseline\n7. Write synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json\n8. If drift detected, publish agent.status.synthetics.drift event\n9. Exit 0 (success) or 1 (hard failure only — drift is reported, not failed)\n```\n\n### Fingerprint Stability\n\nThe fingerprint MUST be byte-stable across runs. Key decisions:\n\n1. **Sort all arrays by a deterministic key** (job_id for top_picks)\n2. **Round floating-point scores to 4 decimal places** to avoid IEEE precision drift\n3. **Exclude timestamps and run_ids** from fingerprint comparison\n4. **Include ordering of first 5 top_picks** as an exact-match field\n\n### Cache Contract Enforcement\n\nEvery Claude API call MUST include:\n\n```python\nmessages=[\n    {\n        \"role\": \"user\",\n        \"content\": [\n            {\n                \"type\": \"text\",\n                \"text\": system_prompt,\n                \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}\n            },\n            {\n                \"type\": \"text\",\n                \"text\": candidate_identity,\n                \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}\n            },\n            {\n                \"type\": \"text\",\n                \"text\": jd_text\n            }\n        ]\n    }\n]\n```\n\nThe scorer module is FROZEN. If it doesn't support `cache_control`, the synthetics-scoring-agent must call the Claude API directly (bypassing the scorer's internal call) or wrap the scorer with cache-aware instrumentation. Do NOT modify the frozen `relevance_scorer.py`.\n\n### Drift Severity Rules\n\nFrom NUTRIENTS.md §I.4:\n\n```\ngreen: zero violations\nyellow: tolerance violations only, no exact-match violations\nred: any exact-match violation OR tolerance violation > 2× threshold\n```\n\n### Report File Path\n\n`synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json`\n\nWhere `<ts>` is ISO-8601 UTC timestamp: `2026-05-28T03-00-00Z`\n\nThe `synthetics/runs/` directory is gitignored. Reports are ephemeral. Baselines are the permanent record.\n\n### Integration with Celery Beat\n\nThe scoring suite runs daily at 03:00 ET. This is NOT wired via scheduler-agent (which is frozen). Instead, synthetics-crawler-agent owns a separate beat schedule extension that additively registers the synthetics tasks.\n\nFor this biome (synthetics-scoring-agent), the CLI is the primary interface. Celery scheduling is owned by synthetics-crawler-agent via the additive beat extension.\n","numLines":144,"startLine":1,"totalLines":144}}}}
