{"t":"2026-05-28T03:43:49.731Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KpmfesSmnYxXEMxTDQazgF","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n     2→# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n     3→\n     4→\"\"\"\n     5→Backend synthetics package for Talent Agent.\n     6→\n     7→Provides deterministic scoring drift detection via:\n     8→    - ScoringSyntheticRunner: Iterates synthetic candidates × JDs\n     9→    - compute_fingerprint: Produces stable JSON fingerprints\n    10→    - diff_against_baseline: Compares fingerprints for drift\n    11→\n    12→Contract: NUTRIENTS.md §I.2-I.5, HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-SCORING.md\n    13→\"\"\"\n    14→\n    15→from backend.synthetics.scoring_runner import ScoringSyntheticRunner\n    16→\n    17→__all__ = [\"ScoringSyntheticRunner\"]\n    18→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d647432-976a-467b-a023-6b583c162bc9","uuid":"9edbd7d0-fbe5-4c88-8ca9-2f0c01e165d0","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/backend/synthetics/__init__.py","content":"# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n\n\"\"\"\nBackend synthetics package for Talent Agent.\n\nProvides deterministic scoring drift detection via:\n    - ScoringSyntheticRunner: Iterates synthetic candidates × JDs\n    - compute_fingerprint: Produces stable JSON fingerprints\n    - diff_against_baseline: Compares fingerprints for drift\n\nContract: NUTRIENTS.md §I.2-I.5, HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-SCORING.md\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom backend.synthetics.scoring_runner import ScoringSyntheticRunner\n\n__all__ = [\"ScoringSyntheticRunner\"]\n","numLines":18,"startLine":1,"totalLines":18}}}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:43:49.741Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NyS4UKc2wnDF9LrgJMC5XJ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n     2→# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n     3→\n     4→\"\"\"\n     5→Idempotent seeder for synthetic candidates.\n     6→\n     7→Loads synthetic candidate definitions and upserts them into Postgres.\n     8→Safe to call on every backend boot — no duplicate rows, no constraint violations.\n     9→\n    10→Synthetic candidates use UUIDv5 under the DNS namespace for deterministic IDs.\n    11→Detection: WHERE id::text LIKE '00000000-%' returns exactly 3 rows.\n    12→\n    13→Contract: NUTRIENTS.md § I.1 Synthetic Candidate Isolation\n    14→Contract: HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-FIXTURES.md Acceptance Criteria\n    15→\"\"\"\n    16→\n    17→import uuid\n    18→from pathlib import Path\n    19→from typing import Any\n    20→\n    21→import structlog\n    22→import yaml\n    23→from sqlalchemy import select\n    24→from sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\n    25→\n    26→from backend.database import AsyncSessionLocal\n    27→from backend.models.discovery import Candidate, RemotePreference\n    28→\n    29→logger = structlog.get_logger(__name__)\n    30→\n    31→# Path to candidates YAML fixture\n    32→CANDIDATES_YAML = Path(__file__).parent / \"candidates.yaml\"\n    33→\n    34→# UUIDv5 namespace for synthetic candidates\n    35→# Derivation: uuid.uuid5(uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS, \"synthetic-\" + slug)\n    36→# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md § I.1\n    37→SYNTHETIC_NAMESPACE = uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS\n    38→\n    39→\n    40→def get_synthetic_id(slug: str) -> uuid.UUID:\n    41→    \"\"\"\n    42→    Generate deterministic UUIDv5 for a synthetic candidate.\n    43→\n    44→    Handles both slug formats:\n    45→    - With prefix: \"synthetic-jr-engineer\" → uses as-is\n    46→    - Without prefix: \"jr-engineer\" → adds \"synthetic-\" prefix\n    47→\n    48→    Args:\n    49→        slug: Candidate slug (with or without \"synthetic-\" prefix)\n    50→\n    51→    Returns:\n    52→        Deterministic UUID in the synthetic namespace\n    53→\n    54→    Contract: NUTRIENTS.md § I.1\n    55→    \"\"\"\n    56→    # Normalize slug - ensure it has the synthetic- prefix\n    57→    if slug.startswith(\"synthetic-\"):\n    58→        name = slug\n    59→    else:\n    60→        name = f\"synthetic-{slug}\"\n    61→    return uuid.uuid5(SYNTHETIC_NAMESPACE, name)\n    62→\n    63→\n    64→# Inline synthetic candidate definitions\n    65→# These are the canonical definitions used when candidates.yaml is not available\n    66→# Contract: HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-FIXTURES.md § Notes\n    67→SYNTHETIC_CANDIDATES: list[dict[str, Any]] = [\n    68→    {\n    69→        \"slug\": \"jr-engineer\",\n    70→        \"name\": \"Alex Chen\",\n    71→        \"email\": \"synthetic-jr@talent-agent.test\",\n    72→        \"resume_text\": \"\"\"# Alex Chen\n    73→## Full-Stack Developer\n    74→\n    75→Entry-level software engineer with 2 years of experience building web applications.\n    76→Recent CS graduate from NYU with a passion for clean code and user experience.\n    77→\n    78→### Technical Skills\n    79→- **Languages:** TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, SQL\n    80→- **Frontend:** React, Next.js, Tailwind CSS, HTML5, CSS3\n    81→- **Backend:** Node.js, Express, FastAPI, REST APIs\n    82→- **Databases:** PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis\n    83→- **Tools:** Git, Docker, VS Code, Postman, Figma\n    84→\n    85→### Experience\n    86→\n    87→**Software Engineer** | StartupXYZ | Jan 2024 - Present\n    88→- Built responsive React components serving 10K+ daily users\n    89→- Implemented REST APIs using Node.js and Express\n    90→- Collaborated with design team to improve UX patterns\n    91→- Reduced page load time by 40% through code optimization\n    92→\n    93→**Software Engineering Intern** | TechCorp | Summer 2023\n    94→- Developed internal tools using React and TypeScript\n    95→- Wrote unit tests achieving 85% code coverage\n    96→- Participated in code reviews and agile ceremonies\n    97→\n    98→### Education\n    99→**B.S. Computer Science** | New York University | 2023\n   100→- GPA: 3.7\n   101→- Relevant coursework: Data Structures, Algorithms, Web Development, Databases\n   102→\n   103→### Projects\n   104→**TaskFlow** - React/Node.js task management app with real-time updates\n   105→**WeatherNow** - TypeScript weather dashboard consuming public APIs\n   106→\"\"\",\n   107→        \"linkedin_url\": \"https://linkedin.com/in/synthetic-alex-chen\",\n   108→        \"github_url\": \"https://github.com/synthetic-alexchen\",\n   109→        \"personal_context\": \"Looking for full-stack roles at growth-stage startups in NYC. Open to hybrid work. Interested in fintech and developer tools. Values mentorship and learning opportunities.\",\n   110→        \"target_locations\": [\"New York, NY\", \"Brooklyn, NY\", \"Jersey City, NJ\"],\n   111→        \"remote_preference\": RemotePreference.HYBRID,\n   112→        \"min_compensation\": 80000,\n   113→        \"excluded_companies\": [\"BigTech Corp\", \"Legacy Systems Inc\"],\n   114→        \"excluded_industries\": [\"gambling\", \"tobacco\"],\n   115→    },\n   116→    {\n   117→        \"slug\": \"senior-ml\",\n   118→        \"name\": \"Dr. Maya Patel\",\n   119→        \"email\": \"synthetic-ml@talent-agent.test\",\n   120→        \"resume_text\": \"\"\"# Dr. Maya Patel\n   121→## Staff Machine Learning Engineer\n   122→\n   123→8+ years experience building production ML systems at scale. PhD in Machine Learning\n   124→from Stanford. Led teams of 5-12 engineers. Published researcher with 15+ papers.\n   125→\n   126→### Technical Skills\n   127→- **ML Frameworks:** PyTorch, TensorFlow, JAX, Hugging Face Transformers\n   128→- **MLOps:** MLflow, Kubeflow, Weights & Biases, Vertex AI\n   129→- **Infrastructure:** Kubernetes, Ray, Spark, distributed training\n   130→- **Languages:** Python, C++, Rust, SQL\n   131→- **Cloud:** GCP (Expert), AWS (Advanced), Azure (Intermediate)\n   132→\n   133→### Experience\n   134→\n   135→**Staff ML Engineer** | Anthropic | 2021 - Present\n   136→- Led team of 8 engineers on core model training infrastructure\n   137→- Designed distributed training system handling 1000+ GPU clusters\n   138→- Reduced training costs by 35% through optimization techniques\n   139→- Mentored 12 engineers across ML and infrastructure teams\n   140→\n   141→**Senior ML Engineer** | Google Brain | 2018 - 2021\n   142→- Core contributor to TensorFlow model optimization toolkit\n   143→- Built recommendation systems serving 100M+ users\n   144→- Published 5 papers at NeurIPS, ICML, and ICLR\n   145→- Promoted to Staff track within 2 years\n   146→\n   147→**ML Engineer** | Facebook AI Research | 2016 - 2018\n   148→- Developed computer vision models for content understanding\n   149→- Optimized model inference latency by 60%\n   150→- Collaborated with research scientists on novel architectures\n   151→\n   152→### Education\n   153→**Ph.D. Machine Learning** | Stanford University | 2016\n   154→- Dissertation: \"Efficient Training Methods for Large Neural Networks\"\n   155→- Advisor: Dr. Andrew Ng\n   156→\n   157→**B.S. Computer Science, Mathematics** | MIT | 2012\n   158→\n   159→### Publications\n   160→- \"Scaling Laws for Neural Language Models\" - NeurIPS 2023\n   161→- \"Efficient Fine-tuning of Large Language Models\" - ICML 2022\n   162→- 13 additional publications (h-index: 24)\n   163→\n   164→### Leadership\n   165→- Tech lead for 8-person ML infrastructure team\n   166→- Mentor in Stanford AI mentorship program\n   167→- Conference reviewer: NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR\n   168→\"\"\",\n   169→        \"linkedin_url\": \"https://linkedin.com/in/synthetic-maya-patel\",\n   170→        \"github_url\": \"https://github.com/synthetic-mayapatel\",\n   171→        \"persona