{"t":"2026-05-28T03:43:53.975Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CcAAKFtXAZXqxbRrEsZbeA","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→---\n     2→# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n     3→# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n     4→#\n     5→# JD Fixture: Strong match for synthetic-jr-engineer\n     6→# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md I.9 SyntheticJobFixture\n     7→\n     8→target_candidate: synthetic-jr-engineer\n     9→expected_hot: true\n    10→expected_score_band: high\n    11→source: greenhouse\n    12→---\n    13→\n    14→# Junior Full-Stack Engineer\n    15→\n    16→**Company:** TechFlow Inc.\n    17→**Location:** New York, NY (Hybrid - 2 days/week in office)\n    18→**Salary:** $85,000 - $105,000\n    19→\n    20→## About Us\n    21→\n    22→TechFlow is a fast-growing fintech startup building the future of expense management for small businesses. We're backed by top-tier VCs and serve over 50,000 customers. Our engineering team values clean code, continuous learning, and shipping features that make a real difference.\n    23→\n    24→## The Role\n    25→\n    26→We're looking for a Junior Full-Stack Engineer to join our product team. You'll work closely with senior engineers to build and maintain our React-based dashboard and Node.js backend. This is a great opportunity to grow your skills while contributing to a product used by thousands of businesses daily.\n    27→\n    28→## What You'll Do\n    29→\n    30→- Build responsive React components for our customer-facing dashboard\n    31→- Develop RESTful API endpoints using Node.js and Express\n    32→- Write unit and integration tests to ensure code quality\n    33→- Participate in code reviews and learn from experienced engineers\n    34→- Collaborate with designers to implement beautiful, accessible UIs\n    35→- Help maintain our PostgreSQL database and optimize queries\n    36→\n    37→## What We're Looking For\n    38→\n    39→- 1-2 years of experience with JavaScript/TypeScript\n    40→- Proficiency with React and modern frontend development\n    41→- Experience building backend services with Node.js\n    42→- Familiarity with PostgreSQL or similar relational databases\n    43→- Understanding of Git and version control best practices\n    44→- Strong communication skills and eagerness to learn\n    45→\n    46→## Nice to Have\n    47→\n    48→- Experience with testing frameworks (Jest, Cypress)\n    49→- Familiarity with Docker and CI/CD pipelines\n    50→- Interest in fintech or developer tools\n    51→- Contributions to open-source projects\n    52→\n    53→## Benefits\n    54→\n    55→- Competitive salary + equity\n    56→- Health, dental, and vision insurance\n    57→- Unlimited PTO\n    58→- $1,500 annual learning budget\n    59→- Remote-friendly with flexible hours\n    60→- Monthly team events\n    61→\n    62→TechFlow is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.\n    63→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d647432-976a-467b-a023-6b583c162bc9","uuid":"2fd5ea35-1498-466a-bd8b-c56e4b0c1cef","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/synthetics/fixtures/jobs/jr-01-strong-swe.md","content":"---\n# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n#\n# JD Fixture: Strong match for synthetic-jr-engineer\n# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md I.9 SyntheticJobFixture\n\ntarget_candidate: synthetic-jr-engineer\nexpected_hot: true\nexpected_score_band: high\nsource: greenhouse\n---\n\n# Junior Full-Stack Engineer\n\n**Company:** TechFlow Inc.\n**Location:** New York, NY (Hybrid - 2 days/week in office)\n**Salary:** $85,000 - $105,000\n\n## About Us\n\nTechFlow is a fast-growing fintech startup building the future of expense management for small businesses. We're backed by top-tier VCs and serve over 50,000 customers. Our engineering team values clean code, continuous learning, and shipping features that make a real difference.\n\n## The Role\n\nWe're looking for a Junior Full-Stack Engineer to join our product team. You'll work closely with senior engineers to build and maintain our React-based dashboard and Node.js backend. This is a great opportunity to grow your skills while contributing to a product used by thousands of businesses daily.\n\n## What You'll Do\n\n- Build responsive React components for our customer-facing dashboard\n- Develop RESTful API endpoints using Node.js and Express\n- Write unit and integration tests to ensure code quality\n- Participate in code reviews and learn from experienced engineers\n- Collaborate with designers to implement beautiful, accessible UIs\n- Help maintain our PostgreSQL database and optimize queries\n\n## What We're Looking For\n\n- 1-2 years of experience with JavaScript/TypeScript\n- Proficiency with React and modern frontend development\n- Experience building backend services with Node.js\n- Familiarity with PostgreSQL or similar relational databases\n- Understanding of Git and version control best practices\n- Strong communication skills and eagerness to learn\n\n## Nice to Have\n\n- Experience with testing frameworks (Jest, Cypress)\n- Familiarity with Docker and CI/CD pipelines\n- Interest in fintech or developer tools\n- Contributions to open-source projects\n\n## Benefits\n\n- Competitive salary + equity\n- Health, dental, and vision insurance\n- Unlimited PTO\n- $1,500 annual learning budget\n- Remote-friendly with flexible hours\n- Monthly team events\n\nTechFlow is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.\n","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63}}}}
